#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:15
#: 0954487626864c0fb4a0be74aca7275d
msgid "Chapter 5 — Frontmatter as a Provenance Record"
msgstr "第 5 章 —— 把 frontmatter 当作一份来源记录"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:17
#: 1250998b7e074bdaab18dfb1d732b1db
msgid ""
"This chapter at a glance — the four questions a trust layer must answer, the"
" two-block split between lineage (frontmatter) and review state (footer), "
"the cultural commitment that `AI → unreviewed`, and the failure patterns "
"that collapse even well-schemed provenance into decoration:"
msgstr ""
"本章一页速览 —— "
"一个**信任层**必须回答的四个问题，把“来源”（frontmatter）和“评审状态”（footer）拆成两块的那次选择，“**AI → "
"unreviewed**”这条文化承诺，以及那些即使 schema 设计得再好、也会让来源记录一路退化成装饰的失败形态："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:55
#: 02a742731b994628b1cb31d9d7be2395
msgid ""
"You are on a video call with the security team. They have the wiki page for "
"the authentication flow open in one window and your Postgres schema in "
"another. \"This says the reset token is a UUID,\" they say. \"It's been an "
"HMAC since March.\" Then: \"Who wrote this? When?\" You scroll up. You "
"scroll down. The wiki tells you it was \"last edited by the system\", four "
"months ago, with no diff. It does not tell you whether a human wrote it, "
"whether a human ever read it, or against which commit of the backend it was "
"supposed to be true."
msgstr ""
"你正和安全团队开视频会议。他们**一边**开着 wiki 上那页描述**认证流程**的页面，**另一边**开着你这边的 Postgres "
"schema。“这上面**写的是**重置 token 是 UUID，”他们说，“但这东西**从三月起就已经是 HMAC "
"了**。”接着：“**谁写的？什么时候写的？**”你往上翻，你往下翻。wiki 告诉你的是：这页“**四个月前、由系统最后编辑**”，**没有 "
"diff**。它**并不告诉你**：是不是有人类写的？有没有人类**看过**？它**本应对标**的、**后端的哪一次 commit**？"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:65
#: d56abaf0b547462db9032bd72c00de80
msgid ""
"This chapter is about the second smallest change a software KB can make and "
"the largest payoff it can extract from that change: a YAML frontmatter block"
" at the top of every file and a six-field HTML comment at the bottom. "
"Together, those two blocks force the KB to answer four questions — *who, "
"when, against what, and has anyone checked* — at the beginning of every "
"conversation rather than the middle of the bad ones."
msgstr ""
"这一章讲的是：**一个软件知识库能做的第二小的改动**，以及从这个改动里**能兑换到的最大的回报** —— 每一份文件**顶上**一段 YAML "
"frontmatter，**底上**一段带六个字段的 HTML "
"注释。这**两块东西**加在一起，就会**强迫**知识库在**每一次对话开始**时（而不是**在糟糕对话的半截**）回答**四个问题** ——  "
"*谁写的、什么时候、对标的是什么、有没有人核对过* 。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:73
#: 7d7ee37c512845f2b7233bced93bc193
msgid "Why"
msgstr "为什么"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:75
#: f7500f6148324df5b3e5f8e7c48ecfd6
msgid ""
"A KB is only as useful as it is trusted. And \"trust\" in a software "
"knowledge base is not a feeling — it is a set of concrete questions the KB "
"must answer, every time, without a human:"
msgstr ""
"一个知识库有多好用，取决于它有多被信任。而一个软件知识库里的“信任”并不是感觉 —— "
"它是一串**具体的问题**，知识库每一次都得在**不需要有人在场**的情况下把它们答出来："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:79
#: 5a391ea01deb452d82f03cc9d3b37414
msgid "**Who wrote this?** A human teammate, or an LLM?"
msgstr "**是谁写的？** 一个人类同事，还是一个 LLM？"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:80
#: 481d943c90154aa0bc5e358a64016079
msgid "**When was it written, and against which version of the software?**"
msgstr "**什么时候写的？对着哪个版本的软件写的？**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:81
#: 620d7a168b88489caf5c2a53ac15e4f2
msgid "**Has anybody verified it is still true?**"
msgstr "**有人验证过这东西现在还是真的吗？**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:82
#: cf42b21f47414c899fc9a6e7f37662c0
msgid "**If it came from somewhere else, where?**"
msgstr "**如果它是从别的地方搬过来的，从哪儿搬的？**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:84
#: db415fac53a34280bea4c798cc0eab93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A page with no answers to these questions is noise. A page with clear "
"answers can be reviewed, ranked, retired, or escalated automatically. "
"Buneman et al. call this the *provenance problem* — \"the description of the"
" origins of a piece of data and the process by which it arrived in a "
"database\" {cite}`buneman2001provenance` — and the W3C PROV data model "
"generalises it to any information artefact {cite}`w3c_prov`. This chapter "
"shows how the prose-layer reference implementation turns those abstract "
"questions into a handful of required YAML fields (plus, as §\"Frontmatter "
"versus footer\" will argue, one HTML-comment footer), and how the code "
"enforces invariants on them so the trust signal cannot silently rot."
msgstr ""
"一张没有答案的页，是噪声。一张有清晰答案的页，可以被评审、被排序、被下线、被自动升级。Buneman 等人把这件事叫作 *来源问题* —— "
"“对一份数据的**出身**、以及它**到达数据库的过程**的描述”{cite}`buneman2001provenance` —— W3C 的 PROV"
" 数据模型又把它推广到任何信息制品上 {cite}`w3c_prov` 。这一章要展示的是：文稿层参考实现怎么把这些抽象问题变成一小组必填的 YAML "
"字段（再加上 §“frontmatter 与 footer”会论证的那一段HTML-comment "
"footer），以及代码怎么在它们上面强制不变式，好让信任信号**不会静默腐烂**。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:96
#: be7bc833c7ba4d4fb0a28c8bccf0d7dd
msgid "What"
msgstr "是什么"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:98
#: bf00570461814d7abdc67b0a38a3be1b
msgid ""
"Every Markdown page in `content/` begins with a YAML frontmatter block "
"delimited by `---` fences. The contract for that block is declared "
"explicitly in the repo, at `wiki-template/metadata/SCHEMA.md`, and it is the"
" only piece of configuration in the system that is *not* Go code:"
msgstr ""
"`content/` 底下的每一份 Markdown 页面都以一段 YAML frontmatter 打头，由 `---` "
"围栏包起来。这一段的**契约**在仓库里被显式声明出来：`wiki-template/metadata/SCHEMA.md` "
"，而这是整个系统里**唯一** *不是* Go 代码的配置："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:103
#: 450ba856028c4c9586127ea729957fd3
msgid "The frontmatter contract, verbatim from `SCHEMA.md`."
msgstr "frontmatter 契约，原样抄自 `SCHEMA.md` 。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:110
#: 331396bf715f473381308a6fbc9263a5
msgid "Three fields in particular carry the trust signal:"
msgstr "其中有三个字段**扛着**整份信任信号："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:112
#: 394e56443ebb41db94706a7ef76eb0bd
msgid ""
"`created_by` — *who* produced the page (a username, or the literal string "
"`\"ai\"`). **Immutable** after creation."
msgstr "`created_by` —— *谁* 产出的这一页（一个用户名，或者字面字符串 `\"ai\"` ）。**创建后不可变。**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:114
#: 4fbef24b0b1740028cac56c455426689
msgid ""
"`verification_status` — *how trustworthy* the content currently is "
"(`supported` / `unreviewed` / `uncertain` / `contradicted` / `superseded`)."
msgstr ""
"`verification_status` —— 当前这份内容 *有多可信* （ `supported` / `unreviewed` / "
"`uncertain` / `contradicted` / `superseded` ）。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:117
#: fcbd7004245e45c5ab33fa706e3ef8d5
msgid ""
"`source` — *where it came from*, if not written directly in the wiki "
"(`type`, `uri`, `path`, `ref`). Also **immutable**."
msgstr ""
"`source` —— 如果不是直接在 wiki 里写的， *它从哪儿来* （ `type` 、 `uri` 、 `path` 、 `ref` "
"）。**同样不可变。**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:120
#: d3df861907144f6cb953e6e556f0d1ea
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The remainder — `created`, `updated`, `commit`, `tags`, `summary`, "
"`doc_type`, `status` — support those three by answering \"when\", \"at which"
" version\", and \"about what\". The full YAML-1.2 specification "
"{cite}`yaml_spec` governs the serialisation, and the frontmatter-block "
"convention itself was popularised by Pandoc {cite}`pandoc`."
msgstr ""
"其他字段 —— `created` 、 `updated` 、 `commit` 、 `tags` 、 `summary` 、 `doc_type` 、"
" `status` —— 用来支撑上面那三个，回答“**什么时候**”、“**对着哪个版本**”、“**关于什么**”这类问题。序列化这块由完整的 "
"YAML-1.2 规范 {cite}`yaml_spec` 负责；而 frontmatter 块这个约定本身，是被 Pandoc "
"{cite}`pandoc` 推广开的。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:127
#: 42865d00726e4004b9809d081317d2d2
msgid ""
"Why YAML and not, say, a sidecar JSON file or a database row? Three reasons:"
msgstr "为什么是 YAML，不是旁挂一份 JSON、也不是一行数据库记录？三条理由："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:130
#: d5a26e8da1a94e1a80a127c3c215694f
msgid ""
"**Co-location.** The metadata travels with the content in a single file. A "
"reader who `cat`s the page sees the provenance without opening a separate "
"tool."
msgstr "****共处一地。**** 元数据和内容**在同一份文件里**同行。一个读者 `cat` 一下页面，就能看到来源，不用另外打开任何工具。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:133
#: 0c25a447dfc8467290a956ab713e570f
msgid ""
"**Diffability.** A metadata change is a line diff in Git, reviewable "
"alongside a body change. Sidecar files split the review across two "
"filenames; database rows across two systems."
msgstr ""
"**可 diff。** 元数据改动就是 Git 里的一行 diff "
"，可以和正文改动**并排**一起评审。旁挂文件会把评审劈到两个文件名；数据库行会把评审劈到两套系统。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:136
#: b0807419da6041f5ba789ad75d25950c
msgid ""
"**Human-writable.** The first author types the YAML by hand when they create"
" a page. Machines read and patch it later, but the schema is still human-"
"obvious, which keeps the trust contract from disappearing behind an ORM."
msgstr ""
"**人可手写。** 第一个作者在新建页面时，是**手敲** YAML 的。后面机器当然要去读、去补丁，但 schema 本身对人仍然是一眼可见的 —— "
"这就让信任契约不会**被埋在某个 ORM 后面消失**。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:141
#: 1f9796fef4bf4ba894767f58b93f36ca
msgid "How"
msgstr "怎么做"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:143
#: b99b2d0267914bf18f7c66f519050121
msgid "Parsing and serialising"
msgstr "解析与序列化"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:145
#: c0a1572af0da454daab94df4c9b7927e
msgid ""
"The code lives entirely in `frontmatter.go`, and it is short enough to read "
"in one sitting. Parsing splits the file on the `---` delimiter and "
"unmarshals the YAML block:"
msgstr ""
"代码全都在 `frontmatter.go` 里，短到可以**一坐读完**。解析逻辑就是在 `---` 分隔符上把文件切开，再把 YAML 块反序列化："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:149
#: ba8b02aa8149490789d23167cb9e74b4
msgid "`ParseFrontmatter` — `---` is the fence, YAML does the rest."
msgstr "`ParseFrontmatter` —— `---` 是围栏，其余交给 YAML。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:155
#: 7af283dc3dea479bb845c4ef3a90fe45
msgid ""
"Serialisation is the inverse, building the YAML block back around the body:"
msgstr "序列化就是反向操作：把 YAML 块围着正文重新拼回来："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:158
#: 9c62ea5ff1d943ab9d3a8465c7d28b3c
msgid "`SerializeFrontmatter` — round-trip with the standard YAML marshaller."
msgstr "`SerializeFrontmatter` —— 用标准 YAML marshaller 做 round-trip。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:164
#: f9ccf98f761442c5ac3ce4fa87ffb4c0
msgid ""
"The symmetry matters. The same bytes that a human wrote can be read by the "
"server, patched, and written back, without any lossy projection through a "
"secondary schema. This is what makes \"edit with `vim` and commit with "
"`git`\" a supported workflow rather than an escape hatch."
msgstr ""
"**对称性**很重要。一个人写出来的那段字节，能被服务器读进来、打补丁、再写回去，中间**不会**经过任何次级 schema "
"的有损投影。这就是为什么“用 `vim` 编辑、用 `git` 提交”是一个**被正式支持的工作流**，而不是一个紧急逃生门。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:169
#: 0bce1c1bc31946708ba2bdf9b7754900
msgid "Inferring frontmatter for foreign files"
msgstr "为外来文件推断 frontmatter"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:171
#: e4102c59d864459d882d774f639c2969
msgid ""
"Not every Markdown file that lands in `content/` was created by the wiki. "
"Imports from `raw/`, files dropped in by `cp`, files synced from another "
"repo — all must become first-class pages. `InferFrontmatter` synthesises a "
"minimal, plausible frontmatter from the filename and the file's mtime:"
msgstr ""
"并不是所有掉进 `content/` 里的 Markdown 文件都是 wiki 自己创建的。从 `raw/` 导入的、用 `cp` "
"扔进来的、从另一个仓库同步进来的 —— 这些**全都要**变成一等公民页面。`InferFrontmatter` 从文件名和 mtime "
"里合成一份最小但看起来合理的 frontmatter："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:177
#: f49e6bf371564ecca8b5fbd0cdf4c572
msgid ""
"`InferFrontmatter` — a sane default for files that arrived without a header."
msgstr "`InferFrontmatter` —— 给那些“光着身子”到的文件一份靠谱默认值。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:183
#: 6e43721a7bd141478efb4e0b4616475a
msgid "Two defaults encode policy:"
msgstr "有两条默认值里藏着**政策**："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:185
#: 8f8724df5c1340df88a9e46ef87e433e
msgid ""
"`CreatedBy: \"human\"`. An imported file is *not* assumed to be AI unless "
"the importer says so. Chapter 6 will show the pipeline overriding this when "
"it knows better."
msgstr ""
"`CreatedBy: \"human\"` 。一份导入进来的文件， *默认不是* AI 写的，除非导入方明确说它是。第 6 "
"章会讲到流水线在更清楚时是怎么把这个默认值覆盖掉的。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:188
#: 32a5ea26a40741e99c751ef279d17950
msgid ""
"`VerificationStatus: VerificationSupported`. A file that already existed in "
"the repo has earned at least provisional trust; it is not automatically "
"demoted to `unreviewed`."
msgstr ""
"`VerificationStatus: VerificationSupported` "
"。一个已经存在于仓库里的文件**至少已经赢得了暂时的信任**；它不会被自动降级成 `unreviewed` 。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:192
#: 017804c172fd46e1a9ddc2a4bc1bb73a
msgid "The trust default for AI content"
msgstr "AI 内容的信任默认值"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:194
#: 2e2630d48f8d46b5b28f6b0ce8535883
msgid ""
"The single most consequential line in the whole frontmatter subsystem is "
"three lines long:"
msgstr "整个 frontmatter 子系统里**后果最大**的一块代码，长度只有三行："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:197
#: 11ec3c341db34f6fb262760acf31c19f
msgid "`DefaultVerificationStatus` — one branch, one cultural commitment."
msgstr "`DefaultVerificationStatus` —— 一个分支，一条文化承诺。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:203
#: 8644d6a24b2945b6b2f6bb9428208fd8
msgid ""
"If the author is AI, the default verification status is `unreviewed`. If the"
" author is human, it is `supported`. This is the policy `SCHEMA.md` declares"
" at the prose level (\"AI-authored pages default to `verification_status: "
"unreviewed`\"), made executable. No human reviewer has to remember to demote"
" an AI page; the default does it for them."
msgstr ""
"如果作者是 AI，默认的验证状态就是 `unreviewed` 。如果作者是人，就是 `supported` 。这就是 `SCHEMA.md` "
"在文稿层宣布的那条政策 （“AI 写的页面默认 `verification_status: "
"unreviewed`”）的**可执行形态**。没有哪个人类评审需要专门记住“要把 AI 页面降级”；默认值已经替他们做了。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:209
#: 37e07571519d41b1b11e06fa3030a166
msgid ""
"The write path honours the same rule. `CreatePage` in `service_write.go` "
"branches on the `wikiAuthor` parameter and then calls the helper:"
msgstr ""
"写入路径也**遵守同一条规则**。`service_write.go` 里的 `CreatePage` 在 `wikiAuthor` "
"参数上分支，然后调用辅助函数："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:212
#: 8acfef6671614625afc9a0e47d2c21a0
msgid ""
"`CreatePage` — author identity is a first-class argument, not a late "
"inference."
msgstr "`CreatePage` —— 作者身份是一等参数，而不是事后推断出来的。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:218
#: 205590f5027d4f57980e62c0bbad489d
msgid "Two things deserve attention:"
msgstr "有两件事值得留意："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:220
#: a44c5c39f7d94fc493484242960090e2
msgid ""
"`createdBy` is chosen at creation time from the authenticated user *or* an "
"explicit AI marker, and then frozen in `fm.Created` / `fm.CreatedBy`. "
"Nothing in the service ever mutates those fields again."
msgstr ""
"`createdBy` 在**创建那一刻**从已登录用户 *或者* 一个显式的 AI 标记中选出，然后冻结到 `fm.Created` / "
"`fm.CreatedBy` 里。service 之后**再也不会**改这些字段。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:224
#: fc00e239b65f4d7981b439bea4838fb7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"After the page is written, the service asks the Git layer for the current "
"commit hash and writes it back into `fm.Commit`. The page literally carries "
"its birth commit in its header. This is `where-provenance` in the Buneman "
"sense {cite}`buneman2001provenance`, and it is what lets a reader or an "
"agent ask \"which version of the code does this doc describe?\" without "
"leaving the file."
msgstr ""
"页面写下去之后，service 向 Git 层要当前 commit 哈希，把它写回 `fm.Commit` 。这一页**字面上把自己诞生时那个 "
"commit 写进了自己的头里**。这就是 Buneman 意义下的 `where-provenance` "
"{cite}`buneman2001provenance` ，也是让一个读者、或者一个 agent "
"在**不用离开这份文件**的前提下就能回答“这份文档描述的是哪个版本的代码？”的原因。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:231
#: e3617ca21e9e4345b4c05a0f193926fc
msgid "Enforcing immutability on update"
msgstr "在更新路径上强制不可变"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:233
#: 302ad250dbd84cc4b4d442d05c7d521f
msgid ""
"An update path is where provenance usually leaks. A naïve \"overwrite the "
"whole frontmatter\" handler would erase `created`, `created_by`, and "
"`source` every time somebody fixed a typo. `MergeFrontmatterUpdate` prevents"
" that at the data-structure level:"
msgstr ""
"更新路径通常是**来源泄漏**的地方。一个朴素的“把整段 frontmatter 覆盖掉”的 handler ，会在每次有人修个错别字的时候把 "
"`created` 、 `created_by` 、 `source` 全擦掉。`MergeFrontmatterUpdate` "
"在**数据结构这一层**就拦住它："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:238
#: 9db75a2427ba4bedbe62de747e07c91a
msgid ""
"`MergeFrontmatterUpdate` — immutable fields are physically copied back from "
"the existing record."
msgstr "`MergeFrontmatterUpdate` —— 不可变字段从原记录里物理拷贝回来。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:244
#: b8d8e91b8e6e4b21ade2aa4557b70a74
msgid ""
"The update struct is the *starting* value of the merged result, so callers "
"can freely pass anything. But `Created`, `CreatedBy`, and `Source` are then "
"overwritten with the pre-existing values, and `Updated` is bumped to "
"`time.Now().UTC()`. A malicious or careless caller cannot rewrite history "
"even if they try. This is the single invariant that keeps the audit trail "
"honest as the page evolves."
msgstr ""
"更新结构体是合并结果的 *起始值* ，所以调用方可以**随便传**。但 `Created` 、 `CreatedBy` 、 `Source` "
"随后会被**已有记录里的值**覆盖回去，而 `Updated` 会被顶到 `time.Now().UTC()` "
"。一个恶意或者粗心的调用方，**就算想**也改不了历史。**这是那个让审计轨迹在页面演化时仍然诚实的唯一不变式。**"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:251
#: 96d359fd2b8b47e3ba68f2df04bc8ffe
msgid "Frontmatter versus footer: two blocks, not one"
msgstr "frontmatter 与 footer：两块，不是一块"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:253
#: babd6f6cd7a2405b933a5b16ed688920
msgid ""
"So far the chapter has treated the frontmatter as *the* metadata record. In "
"practice, two very different questions keep arriving at that one block and "
"crowd each other out:"
msgstr ""
"到目前为止，本章都把 frontmatter 当成 *那份* 元数据记录。但实践中，有**两种截然不同的问题**一直挤向同一个块，互相排挤："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:257
#: 292b176dfe5a48a0b9c1fd986c156b28
msgid ""
"**Where did this page come from?** — `created_by`, `source`, `commit`. "
"Lineage. Rarely changes after creation."
msgstr ""
"**这一页从哪儿来？** —— `created_by` 、 `source` 、 `commit` 。**来源信息。** 创建之后很少变。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:259
#: a97341cd496b4b7caf8f79be59f0f40f
msgid ""
"**Is this page still trusted, right now, by whom, and how much?** — "
"`verification_status` is a single field trying to answer all of that. It is "
"not enough."
msgstr ""
"**这一页现在还值不值得信？被谁信？信到什么程度？** —— `verification_status` "
"是一个字段，**想一个人扛下这一整串问题**。扛不住。"

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:263
#: 2211744f71cc4c9e9c7cbfd69fd577b2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The author's private project-knowledge-base toolkit "
"{cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` resolves the crowding by putting review state "
"into a second block: an HTML-comment **footer** at the bottom of the page, "
"with six fields that every page must carry. This book adopts that split as "
"its canonical shape. The frontmatter stays a *provenance* record; the footer"
" is a *review* record:"
msgstr ""
"作者的一个私人 project-knowledge-base 工具集 {cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` "
"是这样解决这个挤占问题的：把**评审状态**放进第二块 —— 页面最底部的一段 HTML-comment **footer** "
"，有六个**每一页都必须带**的字段。本书把这种拆分作为**规范形态**。frontmatter 仍然是一份 *来源* 记录；footer 是一份 "
"*评审* 记录："

#: ../../part2-prose-layer/ch05-frontmatter-provenance-trust.md:281
#: 0fe5aa7b2dde4f689aebe9ff915fc947
msgid "Six fields, each answering one narrow question:"
msgstr "六个字段，每一个回答一个很窄的问题："

